{title: All Glory, Laud, and Honor}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{+pdf.diagrams.show: right}

{start_of_chorus}
All [C]glory, [F]laud, and [C]honor[**], to [F]thee, re[G]deemer, [C]King[**]
To [C]whom the [F]lips of [C]child[**]ren, made [F]sweet ho[G]sannas [C]ring[**].
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Thou [C]art the [D]King of [G]Isra[**]el, Thou [Am]David's [D]royal [G]Son[**]
Who [C]in the [F]Lord's name [G]com[C]est, The [F]King and [G]Blessed [C]One[**].
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The [C]compa[D]ny of [G]an[**]gels, are [Am]praising [D]thee on [G]high[**]
And [C]mortal [F]men and [G]all [C]things, cre[F]ated [G]make re[C]ply[**].
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
The [C]people [D]of the [G]He[**]brews, with [Am]palms be[D]fore thee [G]went[**]
Our [C]praise and [F]love and [G]an[C]thems, be[F]fore thee [G]we pre[C]sent[**].
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 4}
To [C]thee, be[D]fore thy [G]pas[**]sion, they [Am]sang their [D]hymns of [G]praise[**]
To [C]thee, now [F]high e[G]xal[C]ted, our [F]melo[G]dy we [C]raise[**].
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 5}
Thou [C]didst a[D]ccept their [G]praises[**]; ac[Am]cept the [D]love we [G]bring[**]
Who [C]in all [F]good de[G]ligh[C]test, Thou [F]good and [G]gracious [C]King[**].
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
